Platform teams have changed a lot over the last two years. This issue looks=
 at how.

Section 1. Team size. Most platform teams we surveyed have between five and=
 twelve engineers. Smaller companies tend to fold platform work into infras=
tructure teams.

Section 2. Mandate. The most common mandate is developer productivity, foll=
owed by reliability and cost. Teams with a written charter reported fewer c=
onflicts with product teams.

Section 3. Tooling. Internal developer portals are now common; golden paths=
 for new services are the norm. Several teams moved their CI to ephemeral r=
unners to cut queue times.

Section 4. Measuring impact. Lead time for changes and onboarding time were=
 the two most cited metrics. Few teams measure developer satisfaction consi=
stently.

Section 5. What is next. Respondents expect AI-assisted tooling to reshape =
the golden paths, and platform teams to own more of the model-serving stack=
 (https://pragmaticengineer.example/p/1).

Thanks for reading. Reply with your own experience; I read every response.
--=_wfx_09-pragmatic-engineer
